---
/**
 * Event detail — the Webflow COLLECTION TEMPLATE paste unit for the Events
 * collection. Same DOM as `src/pages/events/[slug].astro` (which renders the
 * static dev pages), so `src/styles/event-detail.css` styles both unchanged.
 *
 * Every `[[ Field ]]` below is a placeholder. In the Webflow Embed editor,
 * select it (brackets included) and replace it with "+ Add Field" → that
 * field. Nothing else in this file needs editing in Webflow.
 *
 * THREE THINGS LIVE OUTSIDE THIS EMBED, as native Webflow elements, because an
 * Embed cannot reach them:
 *
 *   .ct-event-description  a Rich Text element bound to Description. "+ Add
 *                          Field" cannot insert Rich Text into an Embed, so
 *                          the script below moves its children into <article>.
 *   .ct-event-upcoming     an empty Div with conditional visibility
 *                          "Is Upcoming is On". Webflow keeps a hidden
 *                          conditional element in the DOM with
 *                          `w-condition-invisible`, which is what the script
 *                          reads — a Switch field cannot be inserted either.
 *   .ct-event-related-source  a Collection List of Events (Is Upcoming = On)
 *                          whose item holds the RelatedCard embed. The script
 *                          moves its cards into the rail below.
 *
 * All three are hidden by the <style> below, so they never render where they
 * sit. The script waits for DOMContentLoaded, so their position on the page
 * does not matter.
 *
 * NO "+ Add Field" IN THE EMBED EDITOR? Leave the [[ markers ]] as they are and add
 * the hidden .ct-event-data Div described in the Webflow steps; fill() copies its
 * bound values into the markers. Inside each Collection Item, a .ct-event-card-data
 * Div does the same for the upcoming-events cards.
 *
 * Speaker cards are three fixed slots (Speaker 1–3 fields); an empty Name
 * removes its slot. Past events point the play control at Recording Link
 * (the Demio replay) and drop it when that field is empty.
 */
---

